# Talk scripts for the Gero's Lab NPCs (Act 1). Each "list <name>" is a named step list that areas.json hands to a
# spawn ("spawn_talk" for edited areas, "talk" for new ones).
list scientist_talk
narrate Lab technician: Doctor! The drone's targeting array is drifting again... three degrees, just as you said.
narrate Lab technician: If you'd like to test it yourself, the {c07}drone terminal{c02} is by the monitor wall.
list drone_npc_talk
narrate A spare Red Ribbon combat drone, powered down for repairs. Its targeting array has been taken apart.
list gevo_talk
say gevo.0 Get some sleep, Father. I'll radio in once the squad reaches the Northern Wastelands.
# drone terminal: one event per terminal spot. It runs the two-way toggle (drone is the player -> Gero, else the drone
# joins and takes over), then one line that fits both directions. Separate lines per direction would need conditional
# exits, but the engine only checks exit conditions when an area loads, and reloading in place (load_area) loses the player.
list drone_toggle
code 02 15 00 02 0b 13 00 09 00 00 02 95 12 00 0a 00 02 02 97 00 02 02 95
narrate The drone terminal chirps. Remote control link transferred.
list lift_talk
narrate The lift up to the command tower. Commander Red can wait for his report.
